  "description": "[being built] EZGH SSO resource binding (contracts/api-conventions.md#canonical-resource-urls-being-built, contracts/identity-and-authz.md#resource-binding). canonicalize: sso-edge applies it to RFC 8707 resource (null: invalid_target) and binds the result; kits apply it to the requestUrl they send org-api. canonical is the exact output, or null when the input is refused; reason is for people, not compared. requestUrls: how a kit builds requestUrl from its configured public base URL (on a per-directory host, the base the product built from the alias it resolved, such as https://acme.mcp.ezgh.app) and the raw request-target; headers are ignored (never Host or X-Forwarded-*); null means no requestUrl can be built (a bad base URL is a configuration error; a bad path is 401 without calling org-api). match: org-api's exact comparison of requestUrl (null: not sent) with the token's bound resource; allow, or invalid_token (401, RFC 6750 invalid_token, not recorded). order: the binding is checked before the organization (the path's, or on a per-directory host the organization its alias resolved to); not_found is 404, not recorded; allow means org-api goes on to evaluate policies under the directory and scope ceilings. Reference implementation: scripts/lib/resource-binding.mjs.",
